        "abstract": "I would like to thank those gentlemen who have contributed so much useful information to the discussion. Mr. McDonald is to be congratulated on the testing set evolved by him to meet specific requirements when no commercial sets were available. It would be interesting to know if it has been used to test bushings other than the 6$md6 kV ones for which it was built, and if so, what results were obtained. It can be agreed that “a 20 per cent. power-factor bushing need not necessarily be nearer breakdown than a 15 per cent. bushing,” as this is largely conditioned by what portion of the composite structure comprising the bushing is giving rise to the high power-factor, and by the stress distribution. Actually, it is not a material point whether a bushing is 15 or 20 per cent., as it is difficult to consider any insulator with a power-factor of this order as other than a potential hazard.",
