        "abstract": "Where the transmission line voltage supplying a town is the same as that of the town's primary distribution network, the author implies that the omission of the added impedance of stepdown transformers is invariably an advantage. This may be so from the supplier's point of view, but the effect of this omission on the rating of the consumer's HV switchgear should not be overlooked. The cost of installing and maintaining medium-size and -ratio transformers might easily be more than offset by the corresponding costs of the higher rating HV switchgear that may be necessitated by the omission of stepdown transformers.",
